          {
            "text": "He joined a lawsuit challenging new mail-in voting rules.",
            "cites": [7]
          },
          {
            "text": "He helped sue to stop an attempt to end birthright citizenship.",
            "cites": [4]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Raoul created the state’s first Organized Retail Crime Task Force and leads the Illinois Internet Crimes Against Children Taskforce. He secured a $7.4 billion settlement from his lawsuit against Purdue Pharma over opioids. His office negotiated a $140 million cut to a Nicor Gas rate increase request. His campaign says he has worked to expand access to emergency and medication abortion, and his Worker Protection Unit has secured millions of dollars in owed wages for workers.",
        "cites": [1, 8, 9],
